In a levelling-based MMO such as World of Warcraft or Everquest, your
levelling pace is controlled by how often, how competently, and how
intensely you play, and your fellow players play with different
frequency, competence, and intensity to you.

If your play is both irregular and infrequent (say, you play one day
each week, but a different day from week to week), you may well find
yourself scrabbling about for pick-up groups a lot of the time. Every
MMO player who's been around for a while collects at least one "PUG
from Hell" story, unless they're extremely fortunate.
